This Quarterly Report contains certain forward-looking statements within the meaning of the U.S. federal securities laws. These forward-looking statements are generally identified by the words “believe,” “project,” “expect,” “anticipate,” “estimate,” “intend,” “strategy,” “future,” “opportunity,” “potential,” “plan,” “may,” “should,” “will,” “would,” “will be,” “will continue,” “will likely result,” and similar expressions. Forward-looking statements are predictions, projections and other statements about future events or conditions that are based on current expectations and assumptions and, as a result, are subject to risks and uncertainties. Many factors could cause actual future events to differ materially from the forward-looking statements in this Quarterly Report, including, but not limited to:

● | our ability to realize the expected benefits of the business combination (the “Business Combination”) pursuant to that certain Business Combination Agreement, dated as of July 21, 2025 (as amended, the “Business Combination Agreement”), by and among StablecoinX Inc. (“StablecoinX”), TLGY Acquisition Corporation (“TLGY”), StablecoinX Assets Inc. (“SC Assets”) and the other parties thereto;

● | the failure of StablecoinX to maintain the listing of its shares of Class A Common Stock (as defined below);

● | costs related to the Business Combination and as a result of becoming a public company;

● | changes in business, market, financial, political and regulatory conditions;

● | risks relating to StablecoinX’s operations and business;

● | risks relating to the highly volatile nature of the price of ENA and other products issued by the Ethena Foundation (as defined below);

● | risks related to increased competition in the industries in which StablecoinX operates;

● | risks relating to significant legal, commercial, regulatory and technical uncertainty regarding crypto assets, including stablecoins;

● | risks relating to the treatment of crypto assets for U.S. and foreign tax purposes;

● | risks that StablecoinX experiences difficulties managing its growth and expanding operations;

● | risks that StablecoinX experiences difficulties managing its growth and expanding operations;

● | challenges in implementing StablecoinX’s business plan including developing and launching its infrastructure services, StablecoinX Harness middleware and distribution services, due to operational challenges, significant competition and regulation or other reasons;

● | the failure of StablecoinX to retain or recruit required officers, key personnel or directors;

● | risk related to information technology systems, including cyber threats, disruption, damage and failure;

● | the outcome of any potential legal proceedings that may be instituted against StablecoinX or others following the closing of the Business Combination, and;

● | other risks and uncertainties described in this Quarterly Report and the other filings of StablecoinX with the SEC.

The inclusion of any statement in this Quarterly Report does not constitute an admission by StablecoinX or any other person that the events or circumstances described in such statement are material.

The foregoing list of risk factors is not exhaustive. You should carefully consider the foregoing factors and the other risks and uncertainties described in the “Risk Factors” section of the final prospectus of StablecoinX, dated as of February 17, 2026, as supplemented on May 29, 2026 (the “proxy statement/prospectus”) and this Quarterly Report, and other documents that have been filed by StablecoinX with the SEC and other documents to be filed by StablecoinX from time to time with the SEC. These filings do or will identify and address other important risks and uncertainties that could cause actual events and results to differ materially from those contained in the forward-looking statements. There may be additional risks that StablecoinX does not presently know or that StablecoinX currently believes are immaterial that could also cause actual results to differ from those contained in the forward-looking statements.

Accordingly, forward-looking statements should not be relied upon as representing the views of StablecoinX as of any subsequent date, and StablecoinX does not undertake any obligation to update forward-looking statements to reflect events or circumstances after the date they were made, whether as a result of new information, future events or otherwise, except as may be required under applicable securities laws. It is not possible for the StablecoinX management to predict all risks, nor can we assess the impact of all factors on our business or the extent to which any factor, or combination of factors, may cause actual results to differ materially from those contained in any forward-looking statements we may make.

Factors that could cause our actual results to differ materially from our expectations, as described in this Quarterly Report, include the risk factors described in the “Risk Factors” section of the proxy statement/prospectus filed with the SEC on February 17, 2026, as supplemented on May 29, 2026 (“Proxy Statement/Prospectus”). The risk factors below should be read in conjunction with the risk factors disclosed in the Proxy Statement/Prospectus, which are incorporated herein by reference.

StablecoinX may not be able to successfully execute its business strategy or achieve the anticipated benefits from the continued development and expansion of its business.

StablecoinX is continuing to develop and expand its business across multiple complementary operating areas, including Infrastructure Services, Infrastructure Software and Distribution Services, supported by its ENA treasury strategy. Our ability to execute our business strategy and achieve the anticipated benefits from these activities will depend on our ability to successfully operate, scale and integrate our businesses, develop and commercialize new products and services, establish and maintain commercial relationships, allocate capital and other resources effectively, and respond to changing market, technological and regulatory conditions. Among other things:

● | our Infrastructure Services business may not operate as expected, may experience interruptions or other operational or technical difficulties, or may not expand to additional networks, assets or use cases on commercially attractive terms;

● | we may not successfully commercialize or achieve sustained customer adoption of the StablecoinX Harness or develop additional functionality on commercially attractive terms;

● | our Distribution Services business is in an early stage of development and may not result in successful distribution arrangements, financing transactions, investment vehicles or other commercial opportunities;

● | we may not be able to effectively manage multiple business lines at different stages of development and commercialization, including allocating sufficient capital, personnel, technology and management resources among our existing and planned activities;

● | we may not be able to effectively manage multiple business lines at different stages of development and commercialization, including allocating sufficient capital, personnel, technology and management resources among our existing and planned activities;

● | we may not realize the anticipated operating efficiencies, cross-selling opportunities, increased infrastructure utilization or other benefits from the complementary nature of our businesses;

● | our ability to expand our businesses may depend on the continued development, adoption and growth of the Ethena ecosystem and on opportunities involving third-party networks, technologies, service providers and other ecosystem participants;

● | we may not be able to obtain additional financing or generate sufficient cash flow to fund the development and expansion of our businesses;

● | our ENA treasury strategy may not provide the anticipated strategic or financial benefits and may expose us to significant volatility, liquidity and other risks; and

● | we may not identify or successfully pursue additional products, services or other initiatives that complement our existing businesses or generate sufficient returns to justify the resources invested in them.

Our business and operating priorities may continue to evolve as market conditions, customer needs, technology, regulatory requirements and opportunities within the digital asset ecosystem develop. We may from time to time modify, expand, prioritize, scale back or discontinue particular products, services or business lines, or pursue new opportunities that complement our existing operations. Any such changes may involve significant costs, require us to reallocate management and other resources, and expose us to new or increased operational, technical, regulatory and commercial risks. There can be no assurance that any such changes will result in increased revenue, profitability or shareholder value.

Further, the successful execution of our business strategy will require us to manage businesses at different stages of commercialization while continuing to operate our existing infrastructure businesses. We may incur significant costs before generating corresponding revenues from new products or services, and anticipated revenue streams may take longer to develop or may be less significant than expected. In addition, the development of new business lines may increase the complexity of our operations and require us to devote substantial management attention and financial and other resources to activities that may not ultimately prove successful.
